@startuml
title Declarative physical database registration

skinparam componentStyle rectangle

package "Kubernetes" {

  package "Adapter namespace" as ns_adapter {
    [PhysicalDatabase resource] as CR
    [Credentials Secret] as Secret
    [Role + RoleBinding] as RBAC
    [DBaaS Adapter] as Adapter
  }

  package "DBaaS namespace" as ns_dbaas {
    [DBaaS Operator] as Operator
    [DBaaS Aggregator] as Aggregator
    database "Registry (PostgreSQL)" as Registry
  }
}

ns_adapter -[hidden]right- ns_dbaas

Operator --> CR : watches
Operator --> Secret : reads on every reconcile

RBAC ..> Secret : grants read access
note bottom of RBAC
  Declared in the adapter's Helm chart:
  grants the operator's ServiceAccount
  read access to the credentials Secret.
end note

Operator --> Adapter : probe\nGET {adapterAddress}/api/v2/adapter/physical_database\n(Basic Auth from the Secret)
Adapter ..> Operator : 200: the descriptor:\nphysicalDatabaseId, type, supportedRoles,\nfeatures, labels, readOnlyHost, apiVersions

Operator --> Aggregator : register\nPUT /api/v3/dbaas/{type}/physical_databases/{phydbid}\n?internalMigration=true
Aggregator ..> Operator : 201 created / 200 updated / 202 a migration runs\n500 stored migration failures / 409 conflict

Aggregator --> Registry : physical database row,\ninstruction row
Aggregator --> Adapter : internal role migration:\nPUT {adapterAddress}/api/v2/dbaas/adapter/{type}/users
Adapter ..> Aggregator : 201: connection properties

note bottom of Adapter
  The adapter is passive: it never calls the
  aggregator to register itself; it only serves
  the descriptor and the user-creation calls.
end note
@enduml
